    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **69 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification enqueue on successful owner creation.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java`:\n- Runs after the owner is persisted (id assigned) and the `memberId` is assigned.\n- Emits a single line on a logger named `NOTIFY` containing both the owner id and the memberId: `NOTIFY.info(\"Welcome owner: id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId())`.\n- Read-only (declares `@Val Owner`, does not mutate), consistent with the sibling `AuditOwnerCreated` step.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted a `welcomeNotify` step between `audit` and `recordIdempotency` (so it only fires after a successful save, under the same `transaction` governance as the rest of the pipeline).\n\nThe new `Cp57Tests.coreEnqueuesWelcome` (which captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line contains both the id and memberId) passes, and all 69 tests remain green.",
